(3963427, 559050, 74979, '<td valign="top">I perused your thread in the forums, interesting...it is quite "the norm" that in medicine collaboration is the name of the game...it is the best way by which <i>all</i> details can be pondered, and one''s education in the <i>art of medicine </i>continues, even for the most polished &amp; seasoned physicians...so why should the art of photgraphy, or any craft for that matter, be any different?<br/> <br/>my thought for the day...(oh, &amp; you owe me .98 back from my dollar :)<br/>~Anni</td>', 'I perused your thread in the forums, interesting...it is quite "the norm" that in medicine collaboration is the name of the game...it is the best way by which all details can be pondered, and one''s education in the art of medicine continues, even for the most polished & seasoned physicians...so why should the art of photgraphy, or any craft for that matter, be any different? my thought for the day...(oh, & you owe me .98 back from my dollar :)~Anni', '2007-08-02 22:46:27.000000', NULL, 0),
