(3966595, 559050, 51793, '<td valign="top">I read some of your thread and stopped because I started getting upset that people on this site are absolutely ridiculous. I think it''s great that it took you 130 shots to get it right and that you shared it with your team to perfect it. I think ALL 72 teams did the same thing as well. Just because you have 10+ ribbons does not make you a professional in photography in any case it just means you know what people like and have a wonderful camera to take the shot in mind. Creativity plays a huge part on this site and people fail to realize that when it comes to a challenge. I think Scalvert said it best in one of his threads that you have to shoot something that isn''t everyday normal things. "Do something that stands out and it will gain the votes" (Or something along that line). <br/> <br/>Anyway you guys are awesome and I admire "The Ribbon Hogs" Someday I hope that I shall be a Ribbon Hog and just so I can take some under my wing and try to help them become a great also. <br/> <br/>Congrats on your new blue. It was well deserved.<br/></td>', 'I read some of your thread and stopped because I started getting upset that people on this site are absolutely ridiculous. I think it''s great that it took you 130 shots to get it right and that you shared it with your team to perfect it. I think ALL 72 teams did the same thing as well. Just because you have 10+ ribbons does not make you a professional in photography in any case it just means you know what people like and have a wonderful camera to take the shot in mind. Creativity plays a huge part on this site and people fail to realize that when it comes to a challenge. I think Scalvert said it best in one of his threads that you have to shoot something that isn''t everyday normal things. "Do something that stands out and it will gain the votes" (Or something along that line).  Anyway you guys are awesome and I admire "The Ribbon Hogs" Someday I hope that I shall be a Ribbon Hog and just so I can take some under my wing and try to help them become a great also.  Congrats on your new blue. It was well deserved.', '2007-08-03 17:55:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(3966794, 558717, 80878, '<td valign="top">figured Id help with the comments! I love this picture very powerful imagery! 6.9 is a pretty deadly score! you desearve it. I think I would have put the subject slightly more off center personally!</td>', 'figured Id help with the comments! I love this picture very powerful imagery! 6.9 is a pretty deadly score! you desearve it. I think I would have put the subject slightly more off center personally!', '2007-08-03 19:50:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(3966862, 558717, 52945, '<td valign="top">This is a great shot, you have really captured ''despair'' well. The fingers digging into the shoulder help to reinforce the rest of the pose. The lighting is excellent, the colder colours at the top of the frame almost ''descending'' upon him. The only improvement that I can suggest is to leave  more space on the left of the frame to move the subject away from the centre. Cropping more tightly on the right would have him facing into ''emptiness'' more, but then that would break up the shadow which would not be so good.</td>', 'This is a great shot, you have really captured ''despair'' well. The fingers digging into the shoulder help to reinforce the rest of the pose. The lighting is excellent, the colder colours at the top of the frame almost ''descending'' upon him. The only improvement that I can suggest is to leave  more space on the left of the frame to move the subject away from the centre. Cropping more tightly on the right would have him facing into ''emptiness'' more, but then that would break up the shadow which would not be so good.', '2007-08-03 20:16:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3967388, 558611, 60862, '<td valign="top">I gave you a 6, Julianne.  I liked the emotion, and your white hair added a tinge of the desperation older people can feel when alone.</td>', 'I gave you a 6, Julianne.  I liked the emotion, and your white hair added a tinge of the desperation older people can feel when alone.', '2007-08-04 00:16:50.000000', NULL, 0),
